        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(whatsapp): restore malformed credentials from backup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nA malformed primary WhatsApp credentials file could prevent startup even when the atomic-write backup still contained valid linked-device credentials.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe repaired branch validates credential JSON at the auth-store owner boundary. When the primary file is malformed and its backup is valid, startup restores the backup atomically; when both are malformed, it preserves the existing failure instead of guessing or deleting user state.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWhatsApp can recover automatically from an interrupted or corrupted credential write when the valid backup is available, without requiring a new QR pairing.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- WhatsApp auth-store suite: 18 tests passed after the final rebase.\n- Build, vet-equivalent changed checks, formatting, and diff checks passed on the prepared patch.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Exact prepared head: `09b0d55c163fa7a2c800f1344311e40ee6d73724`.\n- Exact-head hosted CI passed: Actions run `28742714587`.\n",
